Backport of mpv-player/mpv#18383, squashed: "ao_coreaudio: cleanup ao on init
failure" (af067b5ea8) and "ao_coreaudio: register hotplug after succesful
audiounit init" (c5d391adba). In mpv's master since 2026-09-01, in no release
yet. Delete this file with the first mpv release that carries the change.

mpv 0.41.0 registers the CoreAudio device listener, with the ao as its context,
before the AudioUnit is set up. An init that fails after that point returns
without removing the listener, and since the driver never reported itself
initialized, nothing calls its uninit either. The ao is freed, the listener
stays, and the next change of the device list calls hotplug_cb on freed memory:
EXC_BAD_ACCESS at 0x0 in mp_msg_va, on the HAL's notification queue.

